Code carried over from other projects
-------------------------------------

The Material 3 dynamic colour engine (src/m3color.*), the motion spring
solver (src/m3motion.*), the desktop palette reader (src/desktoptheme.*),
tests/m3motion_test.cpp, and the Material components in qml/ whose names
begin with M, along with Icon.qml and CohortText.qml, are carried over from
Sung and Tusk, the same author's music player and system monitor, and adapted
here. Sung and Tusk are MIT licensed; the MIT notice they carry is in
licenses/Sung-MIT.txt.


Icons
-----

Cohort uses Google Material Symbols, licensed under Apache-2.0. The license
is provided in licenses/MaterialSymbols-LICENSE.txt. Icons originate from
https://github.com/google/material-design-icons and are the official
Material Symbols Rounded SVG assets at the 20px, 24px and 40px optical sizes,
FILL=1.

The application icon is original to Cohort.


Hardware interfaces
-------------------

Cohort talks only to interfaces the Linux kernel publishes. It incorporates no
code from any of the projects below; they are credited because their work is
what documents the interfaces.

- The legion_laptop kernel module from LenovoLegionLinux
  (https://github.com/johnfanv2/LenovoLegionLinux, GPL-2.0-or-later) provides
  fan curves and several switches. Cohort reads and writes the sysfs
  attributes the module publishes; the module must be installed separately.
- The lenovo-wmi-gamezone, lenovo-wmi-other and ideapad-laptop drivers are
  part of the Linux kernel.
- The four-zone keyboard's HID report layout is documented by
  L5P-Keyboard-RGB (https://github.com/4JX/L5P-Keyboard-RGB) and OpenRGB's
  Lenovo4ZoneUSBController (https://gitlab.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB).


Runtime dependencies
--------------------

Qt is dynamically linked and carries its own licenses:
https://www.qt.io/licensing/open-source-lgpl-obligations
NVIDIA's NVML, where installed, is opened at runtime and never linked.
No fonts are bundled. Cohort uses the desktop's own font.

Visual reference: Google Material Design 3. Cohort is independent of Google.
